SUMMARY:Noon Tunes Summer Concert Series
DESCRIPTION:Reisender will be performing at Noon Tunes over the lunch hour! Reisender is the musical endeavor of west-coast songwriter & multi-instrumentalist Paul Conroy. Conroy crafts upbeat\, moody\, and eclectic synth & guitar-driven indie-pop anthems\, and has opened for national artists including Drake Bell\, Eisley\, and Hippo Campus. His single “Generation 1099” has been described as “a seriously replay-worthy track” by the Bay Bridged\, and his 2021 Album Fmly as “an indie/alt festival-ready collection of gems” by FourCulture. Reisender has toured across the western US as well as in Europe and Korea\, and boasts both an international and local following. Conroy’s greatest personal influences are Paul Simon\, Damon Albarn\, Pixies\, and Paul McCartney. \nThe Noon Tunes Summer Concert Series returns to The Square for its 34th year on Tuesdays and Thursdays June 2 – July 30! From Noon-1:00pm enjoy a dynamic mix of homegrown music from some of Portland’s top regional and local musical talent. With 18 FREE concerts\, dancing\, painting at Art in The Park and some of Portland’s favorite food vendors at Carts on the Square\, The Square is Downtown’s summer lunchtime destination. \nUpcoming Concerts: \nJune 18th – Kyle Glenn & The Wandering Kind\nJune 23rd – Eric John Kaiser\nJune 25th – Burnt Citrus\nJune 30th – Alisa Stewart\nJuly 2nd – LINOY\nJuly 7th – JT Wise Band\nJuly 9th – Mitch And The Melody Makers\nJuly 14th – Sherbet Tone\nJuly 16th – Rose Gerber\nJuly 21st – The AM (Acoustic Minds)\nJuly 23rd – Castletown\nJuly 28th – Fox and Bones\nJuly 30th – John Thayer Music
URL:https://www.thesquarepdx.org/event/noon-tunes-summer-concert-series-5-2026-06-16/
LOCATION:Pioneer Courthouse Square\, 701 SW 6th Ave.\, Portland\, OR\, 97204\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.thesquarepdx.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Reisender-Photo.jpg
END:VEVENT
