SUMMARY:Noon Tunes Summer Concert Series
DESCRIPTION:Eric John Kaiser Band will be performing at Noon Tunes over the lunch hour! Parisian-born singer-songwriter Eric John Kaiser\, has released 6 studio albums\, and many EPs\, including “Made in Gaspésie” which charted #14 in the Billboard World Chart the week of its release. He has shared the stage with the Stereophonics\, Revolver\, Tété and the Lost Bayou Ramblers. After doing over 350 concerts in France\, he moved to Portland\, Oregon in 2006. Since then\, he has gigged his way up through Canada and down through the South\, as far as New Orleans and Washington D.C.\, where he performed as an “Artist in Residence” for the Smithsonian Museum. \nThis summer he presents the “Pardon My French” concert series\, playing with his band\, American classics from Skynyrd\, Johnny Cash\, CCR to John Denver “en français”. \nThe Noon Tunes Summer Concert Series returns to The Square for its 34th year on Tuesdays and Thursdays June 2 – July 30! From Noon-1:00pm enjoy a dynamic mix of homegrown music from some of Portland’s top regional and local musical talent. With 18 FREE concerts\, dancing\, painting at Art in The Park and some of Portland’s favorite food vendors at Carts on the Square\, The Square is Downtown’s summer lunchtime destination. \nUpcoming Concerts: \nJune 25th – Burnt Citrus\nJune 30th – Alisa Stewart\nJuly 2nd – LINOY\nJuly 7th – JT Wise Band\nJuly 9th – Mitch And The Melody Makers\nJuly 14th – Sherbet Tone\nJuly 16th – Rose Gerber\nJuly 21st – The AM (Acoustic Minds)\nJuly 23rd – Castletown\nJuly 28th – Fox and Bones\nJuly 30th – John Thayer Music
URL:https://www.thesquarepdx.org/event/noon-tunes-summer-concert-series-5-2026-06-23/
LOCATION:Pioneer Courthouse Square\, 701 SW 6th Ave.\, Portland\, OR\, 97204\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.thesquarepdx.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/The-Eric-John-Kaiser-band-picture-1-.jpg
END:VEVENT
